vents","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Result\n\nCompose the helper464 GL deletion with **Ali Romman's public #1043 helper470\ndeletion**, then apply **Sagar Thakrar's #3700 OQ4 slot coalescing**. The fully\ncharged conditional BIT coefficient is now\n\n`c = 1736646042038446578551 / 1000000000000000000000000`\n\n`= 0.001736646042038446578551`.\n\nThe next `10^-24` grid point fails. This follow-up improves this PR's original\ncoefficient by approximately **0.001024318895%**; it is an additional commit,\nnot a new PR or a restarted submission clock. The original R437 composition\nalready exceeded both reproduced #1043 and pending #2423 by more than 0.1%.\n\n**Whole κ remains 0.001672660197076918.** Complex supply and the selected-result\nmetadata stay at their inherited values. This is a finite BIT supplier under\nthe stated selected interfaces, with maintainer admission pending.\n\n## Concrete program change\n\nThe R437 word retains 111 SOURCE labels, 636 rational frames, 659 independent\ninput columns and nine paid rank7 captures. All original SOURCE/helper DIRTY\nis restored. SOURCE77's replacement read occurs at its existing frame186;\nSOURCE chronology and the capture windows are checked in both orientations.\n\nThe OQ4 follow-up changes exactly one placement:\n`[6,210,0,8,6,422] -> [6,209,8,8,6,422]`.\nStage6 helper422 joins helper421 at offset8 in idle family209. All 32\nreplicas' corresponding owners are regenerated. Window6 now has 209 five-slot,\none two-slot and 12 empty families per replica. The new whole paid profile is\n\n`{1:380160,2:400864,3:22176,4:26592,5:29376,6:17376,7:26496,26:32,42:384}`.\n\nAll 125856 helper owners and 7814016 emitted local-call events are checked.\nW28416, physical28425, E903456, rankmass1808352, deficit10272, maximum child42\nand halving depth2 are retained. The complete invoice includes the unchanged\nbad-class fallback. Prefix177 bits is charged192, two-level393 is charged512,\nand ROW18355 is below the inherited cap20161.\n\nThe new local-call stream digest is\n`a777373994bd84681d6c2be75251ba6a04a1521580910f23afe09bb50db632b2`;\nthe complete schedule/owners/template content digest is\n`c425a64739981b3ae3ed6b36d1a2f42c2d35e93f007649e89d4c677d8e158fe5`.\nThe word and all 27132 local records remain byte-identical to the original\nR437 construction. Old proof and replay snapshots are retained as history.\n\n## Reproduce and evidence\n\n```sh\npython research/bit-p111-r437-gl464-470-20261018/verify.py\n```\n\nThis self-contained standard-library archive requires no network. Each child\nuses a separate fresh Python cache namespace. It regenerates the actual word,\nrecords, matching, owners, emitter, invoice and exact price; it checks all RAW\ncolumns, rational frames, H1-H5, SOURCE/captures and the historical control.\n`EXPECTED.json`, the package record, source pins and replay receipts identify\nthe current result. `REPLAY.json` describes the archive workflow.\n\nThe final isolated clean-export replay passed all **13 commands in 65.663s**.\nIts receipt, `validation/R437-OQ4-COLD-REPLAY.json`, has SHA256\n`266cdad360452acee74332c9a565fa3fcbe69da197061b24f117380e0a5fc93e`.\n\n[#3700](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/3700) at\n`aa0bd9fbc8700506b1fafcc55bca9bd32aced7d9` independently reimplements the\noriginal R437 word/hosting/price audit. We replayed that audit successfully.\nIts unmodified hosting and rational-price engines also pass on our regenerated\nOQ4 template, including the adjacent-grid bracket. Overlapping slots, a stale\nowner and the old profile at the new coefficient are rejected as controls.\nThis second use is our local cross-check, not an external endorsement of the\nnew commit. Hosted CI and formal maintainer approval are not claimed.\n\n## Assumptions, attribution and next questions\n\nThe inherited all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-SOURCE/target-label,\ncommon-field/ρ/cover, correlated-hosting and precision/tape/analytic interfaces\nremain conditional. COPY uses one paid transform plus retained linear\ncomplete-private-stream discard. The new capture-scope note states the\narbitrary-stream hypothesis explicitly and explains the dirty-helper column\nsubstitution identified by #3700 OQ1; it does not supply a new physical\nall-size realization. Finite audit, CI, admission and a multiplication theorem\nare separate claims. The historical outer diagnostic is not a current κ claim.\n\nCredit **Ali Romman (@aliromman)** for #1043's helper470 deletion and source\nboundary proof, and **Sagar Thakrar (@thakrarsagar)** for #3700 OQ4 and the\ncapture-column observation. This PR contributes the helper464/470 composition,\nthe complete regenerated owner/invoice realization and reproducible packaging.\nPreserve eumemic, DreamingOfClouds, #545/#543/#555, Dylan Crow, DaysSky's #442,\nchafreaky and the full predecessor notices. Substantial OpenAI Codex assistance\nwas used here; #3700 discloses substantial Claude assistance. Apache-2.0 and\nall inherited notices are retained.\n\nOpen work is a new carrier construction surviving every future observation\nwith complete owner costs, and a formal realization of the inherited SOURCE\nand all-size interfaces. Neither is asserted by this finite result.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-18T12:51:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T21:49:42Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2a4705c0f789329f88aaecba831f2d800498174f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"ai-nanachi:codex/bit-r437-gl464-470-20261018","ref":"codex/bit-r437-gl464-470-20261018","repo":{"id":1413965665,"node_id":"R_kgDOVEdnYQ","name":"integer-mult-bounds","full_name":"ai-nanachi/integer-mult-bounds","owner":{"login":"ai-nanachi","id":340844424,"node_id":"U_kgDOFFDfiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340844424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api